WEBVTT

00:00:15.110 --> 00:00:17.950
Mom! Run, Mom!

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.260
Even the people you compromised yourself to save

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:35.510
will eventually die if war begins.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:37.430
Halil Pasha! Ibrahim!

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.850
Now that you are no longer Pasha,

00:00:39.970 --> 00:00:42.060
you are powerless to stop the wars.

00:00:47.310 --> 00:00:49.400
You looked away,

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.820
and closed your ears to their death screams.

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:54.820
Even if I can't stop the wars,

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:57.530
I have to do whatever I can

00:00:58.030 --> 00:01:00.080
with my own eyes and ears.

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.830
We're here, Mr. Falconer.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.000
That's Yeni Tughril Village over there.

00:01:10.550 --> 00:01:12.210
Take care!

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:19.510
When was the last time I was home?

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:39.070
This is where Mom and everyone...

00:02:32.130 --> 00:02:35.420
Altair: A Record of Battles

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:48.490
The Eagle's Joint Struggle

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:10.390
This is the means to contact the spies
I've sent out across the continent.

00:04:10.930 --> 00:04:11.980
A Pyramis.

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:16.440
This is a crystal used to offer prayers
in water shrines.

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:32.960
Is this not how it is used?

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.090
Iskender?

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.640
It is almost time for migration.

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:55.730
Your friends are waiting for the winds.

00:04:55.900 --> 00:04:58.310
With the next strong southern wind,

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:01.610
the eagles will all fly north.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:05.360
I will not be able to use the wild eagles
until winter comes.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:08.950
I'm counting on you, Iskender.

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:11.370
I see you're a falconer too.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.870
Don't worry, I'm not dangerous.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.580
I'm Barbaros the flag-bearer, the kulak of the village.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.380
You seem old for a flag-bearer.

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:21.170
It was a long time ago.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:25.420
In the war 12 years ago,
I was flag captain for Halil Pasha.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:26.970
For Halil Pasha?

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:30.220
You're Tughril Mahmut Bey, aren't you?

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:32.100
How did you know?

00:05:34.390 --> 00:05:36.890
Heard about you
from a man who was wanting to see you,

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.480
so I've been waiting for you.

00:05:38.690 --> 00:05:40.150
To see me?

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:51.160
A kulak is able to spot an agent for Zaganos Pasha
by the difference in the Pyramis crystal.

00:05:51.490 --> 00:05:57.830
An agent's Pyramis is made from Phoenician crystals
specially processed in Venedik.

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:00.880
The difference in the reflection is clear at a glance.

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:07.430
The idea is that a kulak would be able to
instantly distinguish the light from the shrine's water.

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:10.640
Barbaros, what is this kulak you keep referring to?

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:16.100
Zaganos Pasha's spy network
is made up of gozzes and kulaks.

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:19.650
Kulaks compile and relay the gathered information.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:23.190
They also act as liaisons between agents.

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:27.110
The spy network the Pasha created with his chiefs

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:30.990
are concentrated around the water spirit
Nabarato's shrines.

00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:32.740
You visit a shrine in any country,

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:36.040
and there will be a kulak stationed there
in one form or another.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.500
Incidentally, I'm a guard here.

00:06:38.920 --> 00:06:40.960
So then, whenever I arrive in a new city,

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:43.750
I should first visit their water shrine.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:48.970
Well, in the last week,
kulaks have been dropping one after another.

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:51.260
It's the Rod Orm behind it.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:53.260
Balt-Rhein's Minister Louis

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:59.060
seems pretty angry that he was shown up
by you and Zaganos Pasha in Hisar.

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.230
Minister Louis?

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:07.740
I don't know how much they know,
but you should be on your guard.

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:11.780
A deadly fight has already begun beneath the surface.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:12.990
I will.

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:15.870
And this man who said he wanted to see me?

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:19.210
I've already made the arrangements.

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:20.830
You should meet with him.

00:07:21.170 --> 00:07:23.210
I will relay his message now.

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:26.550
"I will be waiting for you
under the Blue Seat of the Triangle Peak.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:29.170
Sincerely, Goz Kulak Baskan Suleyman."

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:38.560
The spies spread throughout the continent...

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:42.940
All put into place by Zaganos Pasha
and Suleyman Baskan in just five years.

00:07:43.100 --> 00:07:46.480
Why would someone like him want to see me?

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:51.280
And only a Tughril tribesman would use
that term for where we are meeting.

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:57.200
An eagle is out on its own?

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.950
Its movements...

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.450
It's not wild!

00:08:16.430 --> 00:08:18.680
Perhaps this is fate.

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:22.770
Or perhaps this is by the grace of Nabarato.

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:26.190
We finally meet, Tughril Mahmut.

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:28.520
You are the Goz Kulak chief?

00:08:28.690 --> 00:08:30.320
Kara Kanat Suleyman.

00:08:30.440 --> 00:08:33.200
-That is Katerina.
-You are an eagle handler as well?

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:37.950
You and I are the last surviving members
of the Tughril people.

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.370
Why don't we drink to that?

00:08:44.540 --> 00:08:47.840
Kara Koyunlu made by the Tughril people.
I keep it for special occasions.

00:08:48.710 --> 00:08:50.710
The smell brings back memories, doesn't it?

00:09:07.810 --> 00:09:09.650
What is your princess' name?

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.610
-Iskender.
-Isk--

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.650
A male? That's rare.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:15.360
That would explain his smaller size.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.080
It must have been difficult to learn
to handle eagles to that extent.

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:26.120
Yes, but Iskender has been with me since he hatched.

00:09:26.290 --> 00:09:29.460
I don't exactly handle him,
it's like we share the same body.

00:09:32.880 --> 00:09:36.380
I heard that Halil Pasha took you in
when you were five.

00:09:39.850 --> 00:09:41.680
Twelve years ago...

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:45.810
When war broke out with the Balt-Rhein Empire,

00:09:46.520 --> 00:09:48.940
I was in the Republic of Florence.

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:53.820
Florence's elite, lovers of art and freedom.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:57.450
They gathered masters of many fields
from around the world

00:09:57.610 --> 00:09:59.740
and endeavored for goodwill diplomacy.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:03.370
Florence had a wealth of the latest news
and information.

00:10:03.580 --> 00:10:08.000
I served Lord Jovani of the Orcini family
as a falconer,

00:10:08.170 --> 00:10:11.250
and we traveled around Rumeliana.

00:10:11.540 --> 00:10:14.340
Lord Jovani was especially well-connected,

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:17.050
and I lived an exciting life

00:10:17.260 --> 00:10:20.510
feeling as if I knew everything there was to know
about the world.

00:10:20.680 --> 00:10:22.390
But ironically,

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.970
I was in Mitland, a place far from Torqye,

00:10:25.180 --> 00:10:28.600
when I learned of Tughril Village's demise.

00:10:29.190 --> 00:10:32.190
I asked for some time and hurried back to the village,

00:10:32.360 --> 00:10:33.610
but it was as they said.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:36.740
There were only ruins.

00:10:37.650 --> 00:10:41.120
When my family and my people were being killed,

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:43.870
I was surrounded by aristocrats,

00:10:43.990 --> 00:10:46.500
feasting and drinking to my heart's content.

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.000
Without knowing anything.

00:10:52.590 --> 00:10:55.590
Afterwards, I did not return to the Republic of Florence.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:58.800
I simply wandered around Torqye aimlessly.

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:07.430
We must send reinforcements
to Tughril Village immediately!

00:11:07.600 --> 00:11:09.480
Yes, Halil Pasha!

00:11:10.100 --> 00:11:11.810
So this is Tughril Village?

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:14.440
Pasha, Tughril Village has been destroyed.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:16.780
It's terrible what happened
to Tughril Village,

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:19.700
but it was a small price to pay to win the war.

00:11:20.360 --> 00:11:23.950
We're here living in peace thanks to Halil Pasha.

00:11:25.450 --> 00:11:28.120
-There's a fight!
-Come on, not in broad daylight!

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:30.620
I am a survivor of Tughril Village!

00:11:30.830 --> 00:11:35.130
Do you have any idea what it feels like
to be the only one to survive?

00:11:46.810 --> 00:11:49.850
Why am I alive?

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.480
I wasn't able to do anything.

00:11:53.350 --> 00:11:55.650
I was powerless to do anything when it counted.

00:11:55.810 --> 00:11:59.070
What is the point of an empty life?

00:11:59.990 --> 00:12:02.240
What am I supposed to do with my life?

00:12:05.990 --> 00:12:08.040
Tughril eagle handler.

00:12:08.490 --> 00:12:11.910
Are you Lord Jovani's falconer, Suleyman?

00:12:12.120 --> 00:12:15.960
Yes, what do you want with the husk he once was, kid?

00:12:16.130 --> 00:12:17.880
I may just be a kid now,

00:12:18.050 --> 00:12:20.260
but I will be Pasha in five years.

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:24.930
If you are still alive then,
I will give you what you desire.

00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:28.100
That was how I met the fourteen-year-old
Zaganos Pasha,

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:30.430
who was a commanding officer at the time.

00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:34.940
A few years later, I was running a general store
in the capital, Altin.

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:38.150
Pardon me, Kara Kanat Suleyman.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:39.940
You're...?

00:12:40.230 --> 00:12:44.200
He had become Pasha, just as he said.

00:12:44.660 --> 00:12:48.990
Florence does not have a strong military,
something you may know from your time there.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:54.540
Yet they have enjoyed long lasting peace.
Do you know why?

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:58.630
They gather a colossal amount of information
behind their goodwill diplomacy.

00:12:58.790 --> 00:13:03.380
Controlling this has allowed them to maintain
a balance with their neighboring nations.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:07.050
Your employer, Lord Jovani,
appeared to be a wealthy merchant,

00:13:07.220 --> 00:13:10.760
but he was in fact a spy
working for the president.

00:13:11.520 --> 00:13:13.140
I didn't realize at all.

00:13:13.640 --> 00:13:14.690
In other words,

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:18.650
the greatest weapon in international politics
is information

00:13:19.650 --> 00:13:23.820
Having experienced the danger
and importance of information for yourself,

00:13:24.030 --> 00:13:27.740
you have the qualities I am looking for
to make my ideal spy.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.830
An agent nobody ever notices,

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:32.750
just like Lord Jovani.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.790
A spy network that far surpasses Florence's own.

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.250
I will establish one for Torqye.

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:43.090
Would you accept the position of Goz Kulak Chief...

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:46.090
...Kara Kanat Suleyman?

00:13:50.260 --> 00:13:52.390
I happily accepted.

00:13:52.560 --> 00:13:56.140
The connections I made during my travels
proved most useful.

00:13:56.310 --> 00:13:59.270
And I used the information, data,
and knowledge I gained,

00:13:59.440 --> 00:14:03.320
to establish Zaganos Pasha's
and the Goz Kulak's spy network.

00:14:03.480 --> 00:14:06.110
I've had to escape certain death a few times,

00:14:06.280 --> 00:14:09.740
but people get stronger when they have a goal.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:14.240
What I'm trying to say is that maybe this is
the perfect job for me. Right, Katerina?

00:14:15.120 --> 00:14:18.670
And that was Zaganos Pasha's very first act.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:21.210
I can't even compare.

00:14:22.170 --> 00:14:26.760
I'm sure there are many people like him
supporting Zaganos Pasha's work.

00:14:26.920 --> 00:14:28.880
Are you not a fan of Zaganos Pasha?

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:33.350
What? Oh, no-- I suppose that is not entirely off base.

00:14:33.640 --> 00:14:37.270
He crushed me at my first Divan.

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:40.900
That man doesn't hold back for anyone.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:44.650
To be honest, there are times when I feel
like I can't keep up with him.

00:14:45.030 --> 00:14:49.570
But he gave me exactly what I wanted,
just like he said he would.

00:14:49.910 --> 00:14:54.700
The power to possibly stop the next war from happening.

00:14:55.410 --> 00:14:57.410
The reason you became Pasha

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:00.420
was because you felt the same loss
and frustration I had, isn't it?

00:15:01.750 --> 00:15:05.460
He and I both saw the fate that befell our village,

00:15:05.670 --> 00:15:10.550
and sought out the power
to stop the next war just as I had.

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:54.800
Hey there, Rod Orm, so nice of you
to come all the way out to the sticks.

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:58.720
You're more agile than you look, Zaganos Pasha's kulak.

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:01.310
But unfortunately, you will have to die here.

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:04.310
Now, I'm not going to roll over and die,

00:16:04.480 --> 00:16:08.940
and facing a woman is hardly
going to give me much of a challenge!

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:10.400
Kill him!

00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:23.960
It seems like your first job as Binbashi
will begin here at home.

00:16:24.120 --> 00:16:26.380
-Let's go, brother.
-Okay!

00:16:26.630 --> 00:16:28.880
Time to end things here.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:32.170
Seven, six, five...

00:16:32.550 --> 00:16:35.340
Taking on three at once was a bit ambitious.

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:36.850
...one!

00:16:38.060 --> 00:16:40.140
Two eagles?

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:46.770
Three assassins for the Goz Kulak Chief, huh?

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.570
Now, how do we want to tackle this?

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:50.190
Hey! Mahmut!

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:53.150
What am I, chopped liver?

00:16:54.110 --> 00:16:56.910
Perhaps this is Nabarato's will.

00:17:00.120 --> 00:17:04.870
This was a village of eagle handlers
that was wiped out in the war twelve years ago.

00:17:05.040 --> 00:17:07.420
There is a flock of hungry, wild eagles.

00:17:07.580 --> 00:17:10.170
You will not be able to stop them with your sword,

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:13.380
Minister Louis' Rod Orm assassin.

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:15.010
Thanks to you,

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:19.180
the Rod Orm learned a few things
about eagles too!

00:17:20.260 --> 00:17:24.180
I hope you enjoy that sheep's blood and meat.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:27.270
Sorry to steal your own game plan,

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:33.650
but you're the one who called the wild, hungry eagles
with that bird whistle of yours.

00:17:34.320 --> 00:17:37.820
What an ironic twist to your own demise.

00:17:43.080 --> 00:17:45.870
You're an eagle handler, aren't you?

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:47.870
How is it that you're being attacked by them?

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:58.340
It looks like you took this hit for me,
Mahmut.

00:17:58.510 --> 00:18:00.220
You won't be able to fight like that.

00:18:00.470 --> 00:18:03.100
Why don't you wash yourself up?
I'll wait for you.

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.060
Okay, I will be quick!

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:08.600
It seems like the Rod Orm
have finally realized the value of information,

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:10.190
but you lack follow through.

00:18:10.360 --> 00:18:15.820
I bet you didn't know that my bird whistle
could make many different signals.

00:18:16.030 --> 00:18:19.780
By the way, that last one warned them
that there was a wolf pack nearby.

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:22.990
Even the wild eagles, the apex predators of these skies,

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:25.580
will flee when they hear this sound.

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:28.750
You would do well to remember that,
little Rod Orm girl.

00:18:28.920 --> 00:18:30.830
Thank you for the valuable information,

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:32.750
Mr. Tughril survivor.

00:18:33.210 --> 00:18:37.010
Is that your payment for stalling for time,
Kara Kanat Suleyman?

00:18:37.170 --> 00:18:40.840
You got me there,
but it also works in your favor, doesn't it?

00:18:41.010 --> 00:18:44.390
I want to thank that boy for what he did in Hisar.

00:18:45.470 --> 00:18:46.770
Well, here he is.

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:49.850
Mahmut, you've kept the Rod Orm waiting.

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:53.520
Let's you and me show them
how the Tughril people fight.

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:57.530
-Yes.
-Am I not even being counted here?

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:01.660
I'm just talking about synchronizing our attacks.
I am counting on you, Barbaros.

00:19:01.820 --> 00:19:05.120
Mahmut, they are skilled wielders of iron weapons.

00:19:05.290 --> 00:19:08.540
Be on your guard,
the kulaks were all killed by their swords.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:10.420
I battled such a sword in Hisar.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:14.000
If we attack from outside its range,
we will be able to beat them soundly.

00:19:14.170 --> 00:19:16.000
-Iskender!
-Wait, don't rush in!

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:23.350
I told you, we won't fall for your same tricks!

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:25.930
Iskender!

00:19:28.980 --> 00:19:31.440
-Let's fall back and regroup. Barbaros!
-On it!

00:19:42.030 --> 00:19:43.370
I'm sorry.

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:46.870
Can't believe I'm hiding here again at this age.

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:50.250
I have made two costly mistakes already.

00:19:50.410 --> 00:19:53.040
I cannot trouble you any more than I have already.

00:19:53.380 --> 00:19:56.420
I will take responsibility and defeat them!

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:59.880
You always try to handle everything by yourself.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:03.550
But there is only so much we can do on our own.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:05.930
We are eagle handlers.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:08.390
We don't just rely on the eagles.

00:20:08.560 --> 00:20:12.310
We gather intel to learn about our enemies,
ascertain then coordinate.

00:20:12.980 --> 00:20:15.020
You may be uncomfortable trusting others,

00:20:15.310 --> 00:20:18.150
but that is the first step
if you wish to accomplish anything.

00:20:18.650 --> 00:20:21.190
Now that I've said that,

00:20:21.360 --> 00:20:24.200
you think you can fight alongside me,
brother?

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:33.170
Hey, those crazy bastards set fire to the village!

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:40.550
Are they trying to burn this place to the ground?

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:48.510
Okay, you managed to draw us out, Rod Orm.

00:20:51.520 --> 00:20:54.940
We won't let you do anything more to this village.

00:20:55.100 --> 00:20:57.150
Now stop with your petty tricks and face us.

00:21:03.400 --> 00:21:07.320
Now then, who wants to die first?

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:09.620
Three, two, one!

00:21:14.870 --> 00:21:15.870
Jump!

00:21:24.720 --> 00:21:26.430
Well done, Mahmut.

00:21:26.590 --> 00:21:28.930
Come, Iskender! Katerina!

00:21:37.850 --> 00:21:39.440
Iskender, don't let them escape!

00:21:44.780 --> 00:21:48.660
They set themselves on fire
so their leader could escape our eagles.

00:21:48.820 --> 00:21:54.450
Mahmut, we are not facing individuals,
but a larger organism called a nation.

00:21:55.040 --> 00:21:58.250
Remember that well, along with what you've seen here.

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:01.590
Now, let's put the fire out before the winds change.

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:13.720
I cannot believe they were able to do this to me...

00:22:26.360 --> 00:22:28.110
The Empire acted swiftly.

00:22:28.280 --> 00:22:33.080
They practically eradicated every goz and kulak
within Imperial territory in just the last week.

00:22:33.240 --> 00:22:37.750
I have to head to Altin right away
to discuss our countermeasures with Zaganos Pasha.

00:22:38.080 --> 00:22:44.210
Mahmut, I am not sure
if I'll get another chance to talk to you again.

00:22:44.380 --> 00:22:47.760
So let me leave you with some advice,
as a fellow Tughril.

00:22:48.340 --> 00:22:53.050
What you need to become a Pasha
who can achieve our goals

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:54.760
is living information.

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:59.770
It's not like you became
one of Zaganos Pasha's spy like me.

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:03.270
Your path to Pasha starts here,
from your hometown once again.

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:06.230
Listen and see with your own eyes and ears,

00:23:06.400 --> 00:23:08.280
and learn more about the outside world.

00:23:08.450 --> 00:23:11.620
Once you become Pasha again,
we should get another drink together.

00:23:11.780 --> 00:23:12.780
Okay!

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:18.160
The outside world I've directly experienced myself.

00:23:24.380 --> 00:23:29.260
I want to know more about this world
Zaganos Pasha and Suleyman Bey see.

00:23:29.420 --> 00:23:32.800
The world that is still unknown to me.

00:23:33.140 --> 00:23:36.180
Whoa, it's Phoenicia's lighthouse!

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:39.560
You mean the Great Lighthouse
built by the ancient king?

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:43.560
Rumeliana's oldest port city.

00:23:43.980 --> 00:23:46.690
That is Phoenicia.

00:23:48.570 --> 00:23:51.610
Ancient cities and new encounters,

00:23:51.780 --> 00:23:53.320
I never wanted to start a war.

00:23:53.740 --> 00:23:55.330
Even so...

00:23:55.490 --> 00:23:57.290
Next episode, "The City of the Lighthouse."

00:23:57.620 --> 00:24:00.960
The chains of pride bind the body.
